architecture={
 'purpose':'M02 converts authenticated immutable M01 definition and separately confirmed design contract into deterministic Program and UiUx generated source artifacts, then publishes an immutable version via one active descriptor. This is generation, not application build/install/release.',
 'hexagonal':'Editor/Test → closed generation commands → DispatchHost GenerationOwner → HOST TemplateGeneration → accepted WORK generation_plan policy. Output ports: authenticated Definition/Approval/Design/Template sources, GenerationArtifactPort and existing FileCommitPort. WindowsGenerationStore adapter implements store/reader coordination; domain has no filesystem/render/framework dependency.',
 'dependency_map':'M01 definition owner → authenticated immutable definition snapshot → M02; M03/M04 single DocumentOwner → explicit saved design capture → M02 typed renderer projection; M02 → immutable source snapshot → M03 preview consumer. No consumer loads arbitrary active paths and no generated code is executed by preview.',
 'ownership':{'M01':'Project UUID, definition/revision and actual definition save. Missing decisions remain Draft/SaveDefinitionOnly; M02 never invents approvalRefs or Defined.','M02':'Prepared generation bytes, preview plans, version manifest, activation proof and operation state. No mutable project definition copy.','M03/M04':'Design content, revision/semantic profile, formal-save proof and single session ownership. M02 only reads authenticated snapshot, never saves/clamps design.','Store adapter':'Safe exclusive stages/sealed tree/readonly snapshot leases; IO owns active journal.','approval owner':'SPEC Approved revision/content-hash authentication, not merely reference strings.','UI':'Review projection and confirmation; cannot supply files/paths/approval booleans.'},
 'mutation':'Only GenerationOwner publishes captured bytes through approved Store/IO. M01 definition save and M04 design save are explicit independent operations outside generation; no hidden save-on-generate.',
 'transactions':'Unconfirmed prepare has no storage writes. Confirm revalidates inputs then owned staging → durable no-replace seal → fresh binding check → active descriptor CAS. One active file transaction chooses entire sealed dual-product version. Failure after seal retains unactivated tree; no rollback deletion of old versions.',
 'approval':'C+B direction adopted historically; exact render/store/reader/integration changes below still pending Owner. WORK S1 source/types/tests remain unchanged.',
 'forbidden':['WORK infrastructure dependency','UI direct filesystem/adapter','template executes expression/shell or package install','generation writes project definition/design/formal baselines','S1 Prepared treated as approval authentication','reader directly reads uncoordinated active.json','seal existence treated as activation success']}
sources={
 'definition_port':'DefinitionSource.capture(project_binding) -> DefinitionEvidence {typed ProjectDefinition, exact codec bytes, prefixed sha256 digest, revision, owner_generation}; revalidate(evidence) -> Current|Changed|Unavailable. M01 existing adopted S2 owner remains authoritative; new UI/S3 unavailable => DependencyNotReady, no JSON ad-hoc fallback.',
 'approval_port':'ApprovalSource.verify(definition_evidence, required_refs[]) -> ApprovalEvidence {sorted approved module/revision/content_hash refs, approval_digest,source_epoch}; every ref must resolve actual Approved immutable SPEC revision with matching raw content_hash. Digest sha256 of compact JSON ["SGA-GENERATION-APPROVAL-v1",sorted tuples]; lowercase sha256: prefix. Unknown/unapproved refs yield missing requirements for S1 SaveDefinitionOnly; integrity mismatch explicit error. Revalidate exact source epoch/content at confirm and activation.',
 'template_port':'TemplateSource.read_exact(TemplateReference) -> verified packaged manifest + all source bytes; verify manifest source_digest and each resource digest, target compatibility, exact artifact set, no extra resource/unknown token. No network/template discovery/install script. Bundled template bytes must be sealed reviewed golden, not a name match.',
 'design_port':'DesignSource.capture_saved(context) -> DesignEvidence {project/document/session/generation,revision,format,semantic_profile,digest,canonical_payload,formal_save_proof}; revalidate(evidence) under owner fence. Initial source proposal requires current captured revision exactly covered by verified M04 formal Saved proof (including pending M05 transfer-before-ACK amendment if adopted); dirty/deferred/missing proof returns DesignSaveRequired. User chooses explicit save separately. Headless/blank UI generation may omit design only when definition explicitly authorizes empty design contract; never infer approval from absent doc.',
 'design_projection':'C1/H2 adopted projector turns validated canonical design into closed UI schema (forms/controls/events/data bindings). Unknown nodes/behaviors/invalid bindings unsupported, never silently dropped. Pending bindings remain explicit disabled mock fields and block executable command generation. Material rendering not imported into first template: explicit referenced assets fail UnsupportedDesignFeature until asset export recipe jointly adopted. No props script/event execution.',
 'binding_extension':'Existing S1 GenerationBinding unchanged. HOST GenerationInputEnvelope adds design_document_uuid/revision/semantic_profile/digest/formal_proof_digest and renderer_recipe_digest. Preview digest binds S1 plan +all source evidence+exact rendered file hashes. Confirm rechecks both S1 validate_plan_binding and envelope equality; no new WORK field.',
 'stale_window':'Confirm acquires trusted input read-fences in order definition→approval→design BEFORE active writer lease, after rendering/preview. Fences authenticate captured revisions and remain held through staging/seal/active CAS receipt; producer mutations return Busy/defer while held, never merely invalidate a token after final check. No lock upgrade or producer callback while writer held; release all on every terminal result. This may temporarily block definition/design edits and is an explicit Owner lifecycle choice. If native/provider cannot express held cross-process revision fences, DependencyNotReady; no check-then-write safety claim.',
 'prefix_boundary':'M01/M02 S1 digests use sha256:lowerhex64. M03/M04 lowerhex semantic digests carried with profile and explicitly wrapped only in HOST comparison where required, never passed incorrectly into S1. Definition/template raw hash, design semantic hash, preview hash and active raw CAS hash have different meanings.'}
